Fillet: a corner of more than two blends whose parse round the vertex
meets an edge twice fails instead of reading past its stripes' surfdata
(mitcad#1926).

A fin's foot rounded with 3 and its top's edges with 0.5 in one fillet:
at the vertex where an arm's outer side, its top and the plate meet, the
rounding of 3 consumes the outer side (patch 1700), and the parse of the
edges and faces round the vertex in PerformMoreThreeCorner met the top's
outer edge twice, so that one stripe stood at two places of the corner.
The first intersection of the stripes trimmed that stripe's surfdata;
its index at the second place still named the surfdata it had before, one
past its end, and the search for the stripes' intersection
(ChFi3d_SearchFD, ChFi3d_IsInFront) read past the sequence's end and did
not return (no result within 15 minutes).

- PerformMoreThreeCorner: an edge met twice in the parse throws the
  parse's construction error, so that the corner fails at its vertex
  (Failure_Corner, the vertex a faulty one) at once.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1711.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_CnCrn.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_CnCrn.cxx
index cadeacc3..4308830a 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_CnCrn.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_CnCrn.cxx
@@ -1658,6 +1658,22 @@ void ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreThreeCorner(const int Jndex, const int nconges)
       SummarizeNormal(V1, Fcur, Ecur, SumFaceNormalAtV1);
     }
   }
+  // An edge met twice in the parse round the vertex (the faces round it no
+  // longer close, as where a stripe's face at the vertex is consumed by
+  // another stripe's blend): the corner cannot be built from this parse,
+  // and the indices of a stripe met twice would no longer follow its
+  // surfdata once the first meeting has trimmed them.
+  for (ic = 0; ic < nedge; ic++)
+  {
+    for (ind = ic + 1; ind < nedge; ind++)
+    {
+      if (Evive.Value(ic).IsSame(Evive.Value(ind)))
+      {
+        throw Standard_ConstructionError(
+          "PerformMoreThreeCorner: an edge met twice in the parsing of edges and faces");
+      }
+    }
+  }
